  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Economic empowerment WIN 2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Women&apos;s Economic empowerment WIN 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective for WIN 2.0 is &quot;To increase women&apos;s economic empowerment (WEE) in Mozambique by identifying, catalyzing, and scaling systemic solutions that benefit low-income women&quot;. WIN analyses and tracks WEE using seven different dimensions. These are collected by intervention, depending on which dimensions are the most relevant and most targeted by the intervention in question. WIN&apos;s main indicator is based on the central dimension, income and assets, which is also aggregated quantitatively across all interventions. An improvement in WEE is counted when a woman increases her earned income and/or increases her secure assets such as savings kept in a formal financial institution.

WIN works across what is called &quot;verticals&quot;, representing supporting functions as well as rules and norms in the market system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Women in Business (WIN) fas 2 syftar till att st&#xe4;rka kvinnors ekonomiska egenmakt i Mocambique, genom att arbeta med kvinnliga mikroentrepren&#xf6;rer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women in Business second phase - WIN 2 - aims at increasing women&apos;s economic empowerment in Mozambique through taking on a markets systems development approach and targeting female micro entrepreneurs.</narrative>
  </description>
